---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About GlobalsBlog — Travel, Auto & Beauty for Indian Readers"
	description="GlobalsBlog is an independent Indian editorial platform publishing practical travel guides, honest car reviews, and skincare advice for Indian skin. Based in Gurugram, India. Learn about our mission, editorial standards, and team."
>
	<section class="content-page">
		<div class="content-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">About GlobalsBlog</p>
			<h1>Practical guides, honest reviews, and free tools — written for Indian readers and everyone curious about India.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				GlobalsBlog is an independent editorial platform based in Gurugram, India. We publish
				research-backed travel guides, honest auto reviews, and skincare advice built for Indian skin.
				Every article is written to help you make a better decision, not just to
				fill a page.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="content-grid">
			<article class="content-card">

				<h2>Who we are</h2>
				<p>
					GlobalsBlog was founded in 2026 by Pankaj Sharma, a digital content specialist and
					editor based in Gurugram, Haryana. The platform was built around a single observation:
					most Indian content sites publish articles but leave readers to figure out the numbers
					themselves. GlobalsBlog integrates free calculators alongside relevant articles so you
					can read, calculate, and decide all in one place.
				</p>
				<p>
					Our editorial team brings category-specific expertise to every article. Travel coverage
					is built on first-hand research across 15+ Indian states. Auto coverage is grounded in
					real-world ownership data from Indian drivers, not manufacturer claims. Beauty content
					is written specifically for Indian skin types and climate conditions — not adapted from
					Western skincare advice that often does not apply.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">Our editorial standards</h2>
				<p>
					Every article on GlobalsBlog is written to a consistent standard before publication:
				</p>
				<ul class="content-list">
					<li>
						<strong>Specific over general</strong> — Real numbers, real costs, real recommendations.
						Auto articles include real-world mileage figures from Indian owners, not ARAI claims.
						Travel guides include actual cost estimates per day, per person. Beauty content names
						active ingredients and explains the science behind them.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Honest trade-offs</strong> — We tell readers what does not work, not just
						what does. If a budget EV has a service network problem in tier-2 cities, we say it.
						If a visa-free destination has practical limitations for Indian passport holders, we
						explain it clearly.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Updated when things change</strong> — Visa rules, car prices, product
						availability, and subsidy policies all change. We update articles when information
						becomes outdated rather than leaving stale content live.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>No clickbait, no filler</strong> — We do not publish vague listicles or
						keyword-stuffed content. Every article answers a specific reader question directly
						and completely.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Human editorial review</strong> — Every article is reviewed by a human editor
						before publication. We do not publish raw AI output. Research, fact-checking, and
						editorial judgment are applied to every piece.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">What we cover</h2>

				<h3 style="margin-top:1rem">✈ Travel</h3>
				<p>
					Destination guides, visa information, budget travel tips, and practical planning advice
					for Indian travellers. Our travel coverage spans Rishikesh to Southeast Asia — with
					honest cost breakdowns, real transport options, and the kind of local detail that only
					comes from genuine research. We cover both Indian domestic destinations and international
					travel specifically through the lens of what Indian passport holders can access easily
					and affordably.
				</p>

				<h3 style="margin-top:1rem">🚗 Auto</h3>
				<p>
					Car reviews, EV guides, mileage comparisons, and buying advice written for Indian roads
					and Indian buyers. We track ARAI data, FAME subsidy changes, real-world range figures
					from Indian EV owners, and new car launches to keep our auto guides accurate. Our
					recommendations are based on total cost of ownership — not just sticker price — because
					that is the comparison that actually matters.
				</p>

				<h3 style="margin-top:1rem">💄 Beauty</h3>
				<p>
					Skincare routines, makeup guides, and product reviews built for Indian skin types and
					climate. Indian skin faces specific challenges — high humidity, intense UV exposure,
					hard water, and a higher tendency toward hyperpigmentation — that most international
					skincare advice ignores entirely. Our beauty content is grounded in ingredient science
					and tested against Indian dermatologist recommendations at every budget level.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">Free online calculators</h2>
				<p>
					Alongside editorial content, GlobalsBlog hosts eight free interactive calculators
					designed specifically for Indian travellers and car owners. All run entirely in the
					browser — no signup, no data collection, instant results.
				</p>
				<ul class="content-list">
					<li><strong>Fuel Cost Calculator</strong> — petrol and diesel expense for any trip</li>
					<li><strong>Road Toll Calculator</strong> — NHAI highway toll estimates with FASTag comparison</li>
					<li><strong>EV Savings Calculator</strong> — monthly and yearly savings switching to electric</li>
					<li><strong>Car Loan EMI Calculator</strong> — monthly EMI, total interest, and total payable</li>
					<li><strong>Trip Cost Calculator</strong> — complete holiday expense estimator</li>
					<li><strong>Travel Budget Planner</strong> — category-by-category trip budget with per-person breakdown</li>
					<li><strong>Road Trip Planner</strong> — fuel, tolls, food, and accommodation for self-drive trips</li>
					<li><strong>Train vs Flight Calculator</strong> — real cost and door-to-door time comparison</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					<a href="/tools">Browse all free calculators →</a>
				</p>

			</article>

